    "designStandard": "저장소 학습 이미지 정본 v1.2 §§1–9",
    "prompt": "Use case: scientific-educational. New project illustration using the attached image as a STYLE REFERENCE ONLY. Create ONE square educational illustration with four equal square quadrants, no gutters, no outside header, no footer, no method titles. The four square panels occupy exactly the four quarters of the canvas. Pale blue backgrounds, clearly recognizable subtly rendered metal pipes and sprinkler heads, crisp large Korean direct labels. Focus strictly on NORMAL STANDBY STATE, not active fire. No fire, no water spray, no arrows showing water movement. Water is dark emerald green (#15785C), gas is blue (#1769AA), metal structures neutral grey. The four panels must retain the following exact topology and meaning:\n\nTop-left (wet): green-filled supply pipe below a neutral grey alarm check valve and green-filled upper distribution pipe continuing to three closed sprinkler heads. Closed heads visibly contain a red glass bulb. Label supply and upper piping '물', heads '폐쇄형', valve '알람밸브'.\n\nTop-right (dry): green supply BELOW a neutral grey dry valve, blue gas distribution piping ABOVE it to three CLOSED heads with glass bulbs. One recognisable air compressor to the right, a BLUE air feed line connected ONLY to the UPPER gas pipe downstream of the valve, never to green supply. Label '물', '압축공기', '폐쇄형', '건식밸브'.\n\nBottom-left (preaction): green supply BELOW a neutral grey preaction valve. Upper distribution pipe empty grey with light blue interior denoting air at atmospheric or low pressure, three CLOSED heads with glass bulbs. A separate detector and compact control box with a dashed electrical signal line to the valve actuator. Label '물', '대기압·저압', '폐쇄형', '준비작동밸브'. No water in the upper pipe. Valve closed in this standby scene.\n\nBottom-right (deluge): green supply BELOW a neutral grey deluge valve. Empty grey upper pipe at atmospheric pressure connected to three OPEN heads WITHOUT GLASS BULBS or heat closure. Detector/control signal can be indicated unobtrusively with a dashed electrical line to the valve, clearly labelled '신호'. Label '물', '대기압', '개방형', '일제개방밸브'. No water in upper piping and no spray in this standby scene.\n\nEach quadrant presents the same viewing angle and scale. Pipes must not have ambiguous connections, the valve separates supply from the downstream system, upstream/downstream boundary is visually clear. Supply and distribution are connected through the respective valve body. Keep labels and essential structure inside their quadrant with generous inset margins, readable at small display size. No brand, no decorative paragraphs, no extra test values, no repeated titles, no contradictory labels. Do not import technical errors from the style reference.\n"
  },
